  "result": "All 8 tests pass, including the three new namespace tests in tests/test_t2.py.\n\n**What I changed** in `kvstore/store.py`:\n\n- **Schema:** the `kv` table now has columns `(ns, key, value)` with a composite primary key on `(ns, key)`. Data still lives in the single SQLite file, and the rollback-journal mode is unchanged, so no side files appear.\n- **Existing methods:** `set`, `get`, `delete`, and `keys` take a keyword argument `ns` defaulting to `\"default\"`. Every query filters on the namespace, so identical keys in different namespaces are fully isolated.\n- **New methods:** `count(ns=\"default\")` returns the number of keys in a namespace. `namespaces()` returns the sorted distinct namespaces that currently hold at least one key, so a namespace disappears once its last key is deleted.\n- **Legacy migration:** on open, if the file has the old two-column `kv` table, it is renamed, recreated with the new schema, and its rows are copied into the `\"default\"` namespace inside one transaction. I verified this path with a hand-built old-format file, which upgraded correctly and left only the single data file on disk.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was touched.",
